## Issue Description
Before the breaking changes i had a query(find) which was giving me results based if the relation is null. Meaning i have a Workout which is possible to be attached to a WorkoutPlan, but i want to query only those that don't have attached workoutPlan to the Workout

### Expected Behavior
To be able to get them same as before with null

### Actual Behavior
I receive all, or none of the workouts

Before ->
```
let where= {
        workoutPlan: null,
      };
      if (!!input?.workoutPlanId) {
        where.workoutPlan = input.workoutPlanId;
      }

      // Something like below
      const workouts = await this.workoutRepository.find({
      select = [
      "id",
      "title",
    ],
    where,
relations: ["workoutPlan"]
      });
      return workouts;
```
And now with new syntax it doesn't work
```
let where= {
        workoutPlan: Not(IsNull()), // or just null
      };
      if (!!input?.workoutPlanId) {
        where.workoutPlan = { id: input.workoutPlanId};
      }

      // Something like below
      const workouts = await this.workoutRepository.find({
      select = {id: true, title: true},
    where,
relations: { workoutPlan: true }
      });
      return workouts;
```

I am using postgre
